<comment>
Bai & Stone 2011 (ApJ 736, 144) -- Section 2.3.2: Damping of MHD Waves
1D, Alfven wave, rightgoing (wave_flag=5 for ideal-gas 7-mode eigensystem)

Background: rho=1, P=0.6, gamma=5/3 --> cs=1
  B0x=1.0, B0y=sqrt(2), B0z=0.5 --> B0^2=3.25, vA=sqrt(3.25), vAx=1.0
  BT = sqrt(B0y^2+B0z^2) = 1.5
  vf = 2.0, vs = 0.5, cos^2(theta) = B0x^2/B0^2 = 1/3.25
  omega_a = 100  -->  eta_AD = B0^2/omega_a = 0.0325

Analytic damping rate (eq. 16):
  Gamma_A = (1/2) * k^2 * vA^2 * cos^2(theta) / omega_a
          = (1/2) * 4*pi^2 * (13/4) * (4/13) / 100
          = (1/2) * 4*pi^2 / 100
          = 2*pi^2/100  ~= 0.197

tlim: actual_tlim = tlim_input * (lx / eigenvalue)
  For Alfven (eigenvalue = vAx = 1.0): actual_tlim = 5.0 * (1.0/1.0) = 5.0

<job>
basename  = alfven_1d

<problem>
pgen_name = linear_wave
wave_flag = 5         # rightgoing Alfven: eigenvalue[5] = v1 + vax = 0+1 = 1.0
amp       = 1.0e-4
dens      = 1.0
pgas      = 0.6
bx0       = 1.0
by0       = 1.41421356237309504
bz0       = 0.5
along_x1  = true

<mesh>
nghost    = 2
nx1       = 32
x1min     = 0.0
x1max     = 1.0
ix1_bc    = periodic
ox1_bc    = periodic
nx2       = 1
x2min     = 0.0
x2max     = 1.0
ix2_bc    = periodic
ox2_bc    = periodic
nx3       = 1
x3min     = 0.0
x3max     = 1.0
ix3_bc    = periodic
ox3_bc    = periodic

<meshblock>
nx1 = 32

<time>
evolution  = dynamic
integrator = rk2
cfl_number = 0.4
tlim       = 5.0     # actual_tlim = 5.0 * (1.0/1.0) = 5.0 code units

<mhd>
eos                 = ideal
gamma               = 1.6666666666666667
reconstruct         = plm
rsolver             = hlld
ambipolar_diffusion = 0.0325   # eta = B0^2/omega_a = 3.25/100

<output1>
file_type   = tab
variable    = mhd_bcc
data_format = %14.8e
dt          = 0.1
slice_x2    = 0.0
slice_x3    = 0.0
